  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "Qt: Make the hex protocol background distinct on GTK platform theme",
  "description": "In GTK3, \"[o]ne notable difference is the reduction from fg/bg/text/base\ncolors to only foreground/background,\"[1] where widgets are able to (and\nmust) render their various elements differently.\n\nAs a result, the GTK3 platformtheme in Qt produces the same colors for\nWindow and Base (and Button) in its QPalette.[2]\n\nWe want the offset and protocol to have a background with some contrast\nfrom the rest of the hex data view scroll area, which has the Base\ncolor. So when the Window and Base QColors in the current QPalette compare\nequally, use alternateBase to get a contrasting color that is supposed\nto look good alongside Base and using the current Text color.\n\n[1] https://docs.gtk.org/gtk3/migrating-themes.html#using-the-css-file-format\n[2] https://github.com/qt/qtbase/blob/dev/src/plugins/platformthemes/gtk3/qgtk3storage.cpp\n\nAI-Assisted: no",
